===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dyew-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|journe}}, from {{der|en|fro|jornee}}, from {{der|en|la-vul|*diurnāta}}, from {{der|en|la-lat|diurnum}}, from {{der|en|la|diurnus}}, from {{m|la|diēs||day}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|fær}} and {{ncog|ang|faru}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɝni/|a=GenAm}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈd͡ʒɜːni/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-journey.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-a journey.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)ni|s=2}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A set amount of travelling, seen as a single unit; a [[discrete]] [[trip]], a [[voyage]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''journey''' to London takes two hours by train.}}
#: {{ux|en|“Don't set out on a '''journey''' using someone else's donkey.” ~ African proverb}}
#* {{RQ:Wordsworth Poems|poem=Star Gazers|page=88|volume=I|passage=Or is it, that when human Souls a '''journey''' long have had, / And are returned into themselves, they cannot be but sad?}}
# {{lb|en|metaphorical}} Any [[process]] or [[progression]] likened to a journey, especially one that involves [[difficulty|difficulties]] or [[personal]] [[development]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''journey''' to political freedom}}
#: {{ux|en|my '''journey''' of dealing with grief}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2012|month=March-April|author=[[w:Terry Sejnowski|Terrence J. Sejnowski]]|volume=100|issue=2|page=171|magazine=w:American Scientist|title=Well-connected Brains|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/well-connected-brains|passage=Creating a complete map of the human connectome would therefore be a monumental milestone but not the end of the '''journey''' to understanding how our brains work.|accessdate=24 May 2013|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170427064626/http://www.americanscientist.org/bookshelf/pub/well-connected-brains|archivedate=27 April 2017}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 December 27|author=Richard Foster|title=New rail freight terminal leads the way|journal=RAIL|issue=999|page=39|text=That progress has taken over ten years and £20 million to bring to fruition. But, as Mands explains, the '''journey''' has been one that HSG has been almost obligated to undertake. "First and foremost, this is an environmental project," she says.}}
# {{lb|en|business}} The [[progress]] of a [[customer]] through a [[system]], often a computer system.
#: {{ux|en|We need to map out the user '''journey''' and make it more efficient.}}
#: {{ux|en|a customer '''journey'''}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[day]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A day's travelling; the [[distance]] travelled in a day.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A day's [[work]].
#* {{RQ:Mlry MrtDrthr|8.7|2|VI|vij|passage=But whan ye haue done that '''Iourney''' ye shal promyse me as ye are a true knyght for to go with me and to helpe me / and other damoysels that are distressid dayly with a fals knyghte / All your entente damoysel and desyre I wylle fulfylle / soo ye wyl brynge me vnto this knyghte}}
# The [[weight]] of finished [[coin]]s delivered at one time to the [[Master of the Mint]].
# {{lb|en|collective}} A [[group]] of [[giraffe]]s.
#* {{quote-web|en|passage=Luckily, we saw '''journeys''' of giraffes countless times during our six days on safari in South Africa.|site=Burlington County Times|url=https://www.burlingtoncountytimes.com/story/entertainment/local/2012/10/11/up-close-with-endangered-wildlife/17366921007/|date=October 11, 2012|author=Elizabeth Yardley Pennridge High School|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230331183319/https://www.burlingtoncountytimes.com/story/entertainment/local/2012/10/11/up-close-with-endangered-wildlife/17366921007/}}
#* {{cite-newsgroup|en|passage=Don't be surprised to see elephants or a '''journey''' of giraffes pass you from this high point. We rode here for a treehouse brunch and encountered a few elephants along the way.|url=https://groups.google.com/g/capocagin/c/mf2H4W-Zd9c/m/3Nz_yRU_AAAJ|title=The Riding Romance|author=Rolande Bragg|group=capocagin|date=December 7, 2023}}
#* {{cite-web|en|url=https://www.josetteking.com/blog/postcard-from-eden/|author=Josette King|title=Postcard from Eden|passage=But Apollo awaits, eager to shown me crowned cranes dancing their mating dance in the morning sun, prides of lions lounging in the reeds, '''journeys''' of giraffes strutting across the plain and birds galore.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240417114450/https://www.josetteking.com/blog/postcard-from-eden/|date=April 15, 2012|site=JosetteKing.com}}
# {{lb|en|AAVE|1700s}} [[Life]] on Earth.

